{"type":"message","id":"002d7e12","parentId":"9da778d5","timestamp":"2026-04-11T09:23:39.643Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] **Recommended questions**\nA **continuous right flank pain** is useful to know — that is a bit less typical for classic colicky stone pain, though stones still cannot be excluded.\n\n**(4/4)** Over these months, have you had any of these: **unintentional weight loss, nausea/vomiting, loss of appetite, worsening tiredness, or swelling in the legs/ankles**?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0ca29368015116040169da1319e63881918e9538dc078c3121\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":309,"output":92,"cacheRead":13824,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":14225,"cost":{"input":0.0007725000000000001,"output":0.00138,"cacheRead":0.003456,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0056085}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775899416983}}
