{"type":"message","id":"035feb2d","parentId":"11ba731e","timestamp":"2026-04-11T09:24:50.007Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering urgent response**\n\nI need to find the answer after all the questions are asked. It seems urgent to address this. I might suggest using a tool related to the kidney pipeline, if that fits the context. Also, it could be helpful for the user to upload a CT image for better understanding. I’m thinking about the best way to progress in this situation, wanting to ensure the user gets the assistance they need!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0ca29368015116040169da135291cc8191b95cbb80bc4cbd16\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp2hNUUFhOb6fI_qrETKAkTjo41glLNDKz-JzPXnN7cyHjCY_eedZ6W3JBsKLC_sZwiwZjkyWJb2MFRT3NFfZXu279dDi-UVhDZEV__fc8_NJ78aUMdPqLNxHzxUvUfMl5Z3nzLZjU7pCdDIV4Cig2-imSlx2iqN3W2RJS0mOlC8f4rSrGL9Ml6ozB16WnvI4CZm_rbYlLrh98gxNToQ4KyXwJQhsj75Bd2atX8Kllmwcb4bxwi1gUA4BY4xEKSHMFyiTl8a8KtHMzg57BtnX77tzBuW6LcCwtclcG3VdmGuAC9iqzJZvFCXkpTJ5JAfFqmoRUwnsvUDfog1VheMFbp3cQzhKheYEPEhzqVFiwffsUF4CLxUwV4doZeRepcwjcBvdW0lgeO1d9e5rh-tsQgzl4ZGbhBNRQ0T7j2TKXbifcyA7aK762QSaxnkSmP-GiyPDV4DzrMSLDxbDqHaWxzraDJAHxFz_ulX_rrcF8MhJT5p8jNZa2GNgEEw2rRwFsjKZcALfbFLO3klx8xP0R_DtOECUe0_XwySw-nYUaFJzE6T-JDsoOT4fWeKMBpdkFC9frC39vEm_0rIhRExSbSPnBpLOarf4zDB54uxSM4M9auL4FJ-WuLssgQBjzUcnGafIoBjMY3o25g26E1cLYcd8nrvPqSr3asNk83-4Kl_xpCPyCT4XqJPNK2D67JfrHrRGeYZY_at5TM-4FnyZ0Dw9IQhjfEeujStYR-Q02qAc7BwWTWSDlW0QBpgY8IaOe91BnypWleNpbqN5EPRUXtwwC7GQUj3v_EVlP9TATwZvodWJVEILIkTDyKjm7HBifwVegC8ji4evc0lW6jXrtvRdrL-DoKJvmC1Lx7ALKfmzHNoeXiSk5lLqbooyTf85jlnKZnqwDDidaZGk6CGUfl99deofcNXUa0duVWNQbZZYL8tlIBtwU6EioQRFyZpFgPTMsCL2FjW0cqdCxatET-kNcHg==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Considering urgent response**\\n\\nI need to find the answer after all the questions are asked. It seems urgent to address this. I might suggest using a tool related to the kidney pipeline, if that fits the context. Also, it could be helpful for the user to upload a CT image for better understanding. I’m thinking about the best way to progress in this situation, wanting to ensure the user gets the assistance they need!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] **Clinical picture**\nYou have **progressively worsening continuous pain in the right flank/back**, **visible pink-to-red urine on some days**, **painful urination**, **marked fatigue**, and **about 28 kg of unintentional weight loss over 3 months**. From your structured record, there is already a history of **renal cell carcinoma follow-up**, **post-nephrectomy monitoring**, prior **mild hematuria**, and mildly reduced kidney function (**creatinine 1.4 mg/dL, eGFR 61 mL/min/1.73m²**). Taken together, this is a **concerning kidney/urinary tract picture** and should not be treated as routine back pain.\n\n**Most likely possibilities**\n1. **A serious kidney/urinary tract process that needs urgent medical assessment**\nThe strongest reasons are the **gross hematuria, painful urination, right flank pain, fatigue, and major unintentional weight loss**. This could reflect obstruction, infection, bleeding, stone disease, or another structural urinary tract problem.\n\n2. **Recurrence/progression of a kidney malignancy or another urinary tract malignancy**\nI cannot diagnose that from chat alone, but with your prior **RCC follow-up history** plus **hematuria and major weight loss**, this becomes an important possibility that needs prompt imaging and clinician review.\n\n3. **Complication affecting the remaining kidney or urinary drainage**\nBecause your record mentions **post-nephrectomy follow-up** and monitoring of kidney function decline, pain plus urinary symptoms could indicate a problem that is putting stress on kidney function.\n\n4. **Stone disease**\nThis remains possible because stones can cause blood in the urine, painful urination, and flank pain, although your **continuous pain and significant weight loss** make me more concerned that there may be more than a simple uncomplicated stone.\n\n**Confidence / uncertainty note**\nI am **not confident this is benign**, and I do think you need **urgent in-person evaluation**. The symptom pattern strongly supports a real urinary/kidney problem, but chat cannot tell whether the main issue is infection, obstruction, recurrent tumor, stone disease, or another structural problem. You likely need **urinalysis, blood tests, kidney function check, and imaging** to clarify this quickly.\n\n**Red flags / urgent concerns**\nYour **visible blood in urine**, **painful urination**, **persistent unilateral flank pain**, and especially **28 kg unintentional weight loss** are red flags. Because of that combination — and your kidney cancer history — I would recommend **same-day urgent assessment**, ideally **today**. If you develop **fever/chills, vomiting, inability to pass urine, severe worsening pain, weakness/fainting, shortness of breath, or heavy bleeding/clots in the urine**, go to the **ER immediately**.\n\nGiven the concern for a kidney-focused problem, one useful next step after medical review is the **kidney imaging pipeline** if you have a **new CT scan image** available to upload. If you do get a CT image, you can send it here and I can help run that specialized kidney analysis tool as a **preliminary signal only, not a diagnosis**.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0ca29368015116040169da1354ab3c8191aefb590b4dacbf56\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":290,"output":692,"cacheRead":14080,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15062,"cost":{"input":0.0007250000000000001,"output":0.01038,"cacheRead":0.0035199999999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.014624999999999999}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775899473617}}
{"type":"message","id":"b8a99b7a","parentId":"035feb2d","timestamp":"2026-04-11T09:25:48.778Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[media attached: /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/file_3---a313343f-5c6d-43a1-ba04-5025dd99ac16.jpg (image/jpeg) | /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/file_3---a313343f-5c6d-43a1-ba04-5025dd99ac16.jpg]\nTo send an image back, prefer the message tool (media/path/filePath). If you must inline, use MEDIA:https://example.com/image.jpg (spaces ok, quote if needed) or a safe relative path like MEDIA:./image.jpg. Avoid absolute paths (MEDIA:/...) and ~ paths — they are blocked for security. Keep caption in the text body.\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"217\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"567556397\",\n  \"sender\": \"Andrea Pitrone\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Sat 2026-04-11 09:25 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"Andrea Pitrone (567556397)\",\n  \"id\": \"567556397\",\n  \"name\": \"Andrea Pitrone\",\n  \"username\": \"pitro_eng_guitarist\"\n}\n```\n\nHere it is the CT scan"},{"type":"image","data":"","mimeType":"image/jpeg"}],"timestamp":1775899548776}}
{"type":"message","id":"57701c57","parentId":"b8a99b7a","timestamp":"2026-04-11T09:25:52.416Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0ca29368015116040169da139ea7308191a46c31e5603172ed\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp2hOfNPRA0Tn9nOBNWcTLwp99ac7ehbJmszhAoP5KQHyIMLqMSq0aXFh-jfZboXLgAlE-m_XUZ_k-gA0ZtauNSOm_nnfSyizgrG-Io-p5PasIPv698PxlW3kOeptIIvYFaql98UhnCAiazC2Px22C8Fmn9Kabt8RdAeV8chPXxnBJPE8MzKZHFr53GC0yZkP3RjKcvYryM_3fb_6dPXSCoyKpQF9UIXdwGfCkzd-GV_9vdQQ1Gl1omCJ9pRgvnWBLdNuOceoljIqiiNRGQrxtc_2GUef1UDMF_UtDr3pYg1uA-VtiEw6LV4PKlPNtA0-W_78N09BfD15Ts1CX9ilLTUDU2Mgf_0eh6oRREhEUIXWnYvtS31vilbG34jkrgWTMJzjfjMyUgVpWYpkH-Fy52Ih6yg_F-XwCnrCnw-L7bB4LXrQ-jw47zrZ8kyb-O_fKSMX18WufYxnK828OkV2hyvURgT-l5Cj0Bzjh3jgfi-EQYZmKbfoKv7JMeAsakh66FdBKD4TMxIFmBj9ERPoUOv-BLCXn4SY-HaOGp8qsP1m_jWS11jtQCJXNp_7JBspGTqU6YhibefGkMdZYQrziD_EiBfhBwag4vqkR-elpbDTSYTaso8Jok0LzjUy78HkGXZhtI0pUwN3HQndlXwdBsQ0qX3WcUi6fZdxkPTjcz49UL-CtVPYvcyrCgVaWDVR4c-Hhx1KOL5kgKb2YZR8n-9Brds9pC5ojnrsbYWvu91-oQYxSinOur1C3oPqzkzswtBHcC0tCwHX177KKHznzGgh6ETkB5EaQAiWbBVordviRFOhjShPk5OE462I7C3bfbZlA_0K9HtyaL-K5-NxrS-8x1RElgo_gG04HijyHGj3wlFKn_2aBBd7oI0G2fTrPH0USL8Rr3PEkrlJkaUweCS1w8g==\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"I can run the kidney imaging pipeline on the new CT image you just uploaded. After that I’ll summarize the detector, image analysis, and downstream interpretation clearly.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0ca29368015116040169da139f2d188191b3d588e25f99bb5a\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_cEBO1HdsMaLrrQ5n3agqkPGh|fc_0ca29368015116040169da139fd5248191be366486fcc300fa","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"~/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"~/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/SKILL.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":15634,"output":92,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15726,"cost":{"input":0.039085,"output":0.00138,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.040465}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775899548777}}
{"type":"message","id":"f8faa633","parentId":"57701c57","timestamp":"2026-04-11T09:25:52.426Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_cEBO1HdsMaLrrQ5n3agqkPGh|fc_0ca29368015116040169da139fd5248191be366486fcc300fa","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: kidney-pipeline-execution\ndescription: Execute the kidney cancer CT pipeline by uploading a user-provided kidney CT image, taking the real uploaded image path returned by the upload endpoint, replacing the image-path placeholder inside the fixed prototype request JSON, then sending that request to the kidney pipeline execution endpoint and summarizing the Kidney Cancer Detector, Image Analyzer, and X-AI outputs. Use when a user wants to run the integrated kidney pipeline on a CT scan image and inspect either the raw response or a clean summary of the main outputs.\n---\n\n# Kidney Pipeline Execution\n\nUpload the user image first, use the returned upload path in the fixed request template, then execute the kidney pipeline.\n\n## Required behavior\n\nFollow this sequence exactly:\n\n1. Determine the local CT image to analyze.\n   - Prefer the explicit user-provided local image path.\n   - If no path is provided, use the newest supported image under `/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound`.\n2. Require the Telegram user id.\n   - Pass it as `--telegram-user-id` or set `TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.\n   - Use that value as the upload request's `user_id` query parameter.\n3. Upload the image with `POST multipart/form-data` to:\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload%2F&user_id=<telegram-user-id>`\n4. Read the upload response JSON.\n   - Build the real remote image path as `path + filename`.\n   - Use the returned path from the upload response only.\n   - Do not keep example paths, stale upload paths, or unresolved placeholders in the executed request.\n5. Load `references/request-template.json`.\n6. Replace every <image-path-here> placeholder in the template with the real uploaded image path (rows 56, 208, 305, 371, 396).\n7. Send the resulting JSON payload to:\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\n8. Read the pipeline response and summarize it by module:\n   - Kidney Cancer Detector\n   - Image Analyzer\n   - X-AI\n9. If the analyzer image URL exists at `response.workflows[0].branches[0].nodes[0].children[0].children[0].tracking.parameters.file_path`, extract the URL and include the image in the normal reply.\n10. Do not send out-of-band Telegram messages from the script.\n\n## Fixed values\n\nKeep these values fixed:\n- `storage_ref`: `nodes_bucket`\n- `local_file_path`: `upload/`\n- execution endpoint: `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\n- request template: `references/request-template.json`\n\n## Implementation notes\n\n- Treat the request template as a fixed prototype payload, but always inject the freshly uploaded image path before execution.\n- Fail loudly if `<image_path_here>` remains anywhere in the payload after replacement.\n- If template fields such as `filename`, `pdf_path`, or `File Path` contain placeholder or stale upload-path values, replace them with the fresh uploaded image path before execution.\n- Preserve the response wrapper shape returned by the script.\n- If the endpoint returns non-JSON text, return that text as the `response` value.\n\n## Preferred script\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/pipeline_execution_tool.py --telegram-user-id <telegram-user-id> [local-image-path]\n```\n\nIf `local-image-path` is omitted, the script should select the newest supported image from `/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound`.\n\n## Summary fields to prioritize\n\nWhen present, summarize these fields first.\n\n### Kidney Cancer Detector\n- `Inference time`\n- `classes`\n- `confidence`\n\n### Image Analyzer\n- `cam_metrics`\n- `prediction`\n- `cam_explanation`\n- `file_path` when useful for returning the analyzer image\n\nWhen `cam_metrics` is present, include all available subfields such as:\n- `coverage`\n- `center_ratio`\n- `lr_asym`\n- `tb_asym`\n\n### X-AI\n- `confidence_interpretation`\n- `recommended_next_steps`\n- `references`\n- `summary`\n- `visual_evidence`\n\nPreserve list order for `recommended_next_steps`.\nPreserve available fields in each reference item such as `title`, `author`, `year`, and `url`.\n\n## User-facing reply rules\n\n- Group the result into the three modules.\n- Use readable labels instead of raw JSON paths.\n- Do not include low-level execution metadata by default.\n- Mention clearly that the pipeline output is a preliminary signal, not a diagnosis.\n- Append the analyzer image itself when an analyzer image URL is available.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1775899552422}}
{"type":"message","id":"cec856aa","parentId":"f8faa633","timestamp":"2026-04-11T09:25:56.413Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Running script for Telegram**\n\nI need to run a script using the Telegram user ID 567556397 and a local image path. It looks like the image might be a JPG, rather than an actual CT DICOM file, but that's okay. I’m considering if I need to read the script beforehand, but it might not be necessary. My plan is to execute it directly, which should streamline the process for me!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0ca29368015116040169da13a17b6081919e4c2dd3492feaa1\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp2hOjjiNXVK3ZYcfMJbImkXOdsjIcbMFslLeHSMjZB7ypmvQde73mjRkSBMN-odSkKfdNeO2HD73P3PVv9YMc5B8w3cOcAa4MNqHDz7aq-IZpw-zFPfEFt-HRM2GloMg20Y5LIjBqMMFrUXW_H-ny4Qn4Qpgzp0aY0lwQL-6_gZyIRGyeMHKLwhmbb4ICIQmBTBYS_-ENmM9MiYy-9vpnrgXbELWEvsK7lzMp2VJScQPjdi9OwK2gsW1yl1ZE-_6Yf9xw7VnhP0g--z5IYZTvKAKXmXGgYbC0YGQuB-qG2u8wPWukM3Bc3JiXwaWkFMYKDNlt_1NZJtCiMMjWSJIuRn7Dm_kE_-tT5PuqnOy8NI1h_tu8CeDNO7sBdjU2FEEMgS-9oJ1CKGJCFHWU-3RFfeZPUJSQXrpuau82HyVQnXbs5wIL5shwU8zLJbbx9iAY9rUK7UWFEdGZkAM3yAcGtLTlZNwZ4MFn7DcW_pJMbR11XlvwXvwibyaMbHRknYIh5qFqGHSogZotNP0Nhvi7aEFr_u6--KciLLthe7kxSbIccz48SMvzWiKu92OZ4OOwA1CYE__hbE4aHB4q-8tuXkO2EY5UA9a2LdWv-xyrd1YveBOkI-3KiMuo3d7A_j7RHXWMfcVp4Kqt3uZUVelb-uwKPcPBiWB5Wfnui7TrYY4l_K6auMY8edVvKRUf4r1tvijJLmEjU1DfpjM7THBlPhRQrhaD25tS_Ynaq_D8D8WfLqTqb6f6TxP4pYLP7DLAmBkOfxCCCFCF5ESRTO9JFiVj5e8wFnls_IC3HLL0jtpcLc0smAWjtpzGv-OlxNRel0DS4UwMif3E167pD1TL6cDeiZ7FuqjbuWdAmi6ZcYUCX3UuF5-PVAsKs5s1Nkq3jxk3Qsg-5hi8ZUWEUDr9M_5FmaPTCnXaTwN-VoTTBuo--szRTn49u38gb-jpWW8ZEpBi4VHbz6uNM2Mcho95_gog695xvEwT7pF6sLczkcaCAlVxV-XF6Vg3kOt4nH1dMzTsT2kQDwF4yFauyZ8RnLkife1qwZECWpJaPKCoqy8JrQw=\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Running script for Telegram**\\n\\nI need to run a script using the Telegram user ID 567556397 and a local image path. It looks like the image might be a JPG, rather than an actual C