ore I proceed. It'd be better if I organize everything nice and neat — I really don't want any surprises! Let's make sure I cover all my bases.\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_WT5Uo4F7FFXjDEnau2UrKfY8|fc_0ca29368015116040169da13f6f9848191ab2e7612fec8b223","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/tmp/health_context.txt","content":"Patient reports progressive exhaustion over the last few months, persistent continuous dull pain in the right lower back/right flank, visible pink-to-red urine on some days, painful urination, and about 28 kg of unintentional weight loss over 3 months. Fever is uncertain and no definite chills reported. Structured patient knowledge base for P-001 shows renal cell carcinoma follow-up, post-nephrectomy follow-up, prior mild hematuria, creatinine 1.4 mg/dL, eGFR 61 mL/min/1.73m², prescribed Sunitinib 50 mg daily, and family history of renal cell carcinoma in a maternal uncle. Clinical concern already discussed: serious kidney/urinary tract process including possible recurrence/progression, obstruction, infection, stone disease, or urinary tract malignancy. Red flags present: gross hematuria, painful urination, persistent unilateral flank pain, marked fatigue, and major unintentional weight loss."},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/tmp/health_context.txt\",\"content\":\"Patient reports progressive exhaustion over the last few months, persistent continuous dull pain in the right lower back/right flank, visible pink-to-red urine on some days, painful urination, and about 28 kg of unintentional weight loss over 3 months. Fever is uncertain and no definite chills reported. Structured patient knowledge base for P-001 shows renal cell carcinoma follow-up, post-nephrectomy follow-up, prior mild hematuria, creatinine 1.4 mg/dL, eGFR 61 mL/min/1.73m², prescribed Sunitinib 50 mg daily, and family history of renal cell carcinoma in a maternal uncle. Clinical concern already discussed: serious kidney/urinary tract process including possible recurrence