{"type":"message","id":"d1cf344a","parentId":"ae2ab147","timestamp":"2026-04-11T09:27:37.785Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0ca29368015116040169da140034948191a9b13414af8f33e8\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABp2hQCoJbVvPk3wD4g9v1_DuStUTvDmZMzFO5DqP1ZTuuBjsKkhQJbBdhLlOdEAnBbJXHUAGz-4Gtmpt-qnhlA8ELRFTYfmPJrb7Y0OXPsBO9W6ps1SE4Sd4hRZzZ-j0XR7Ep1Cgsmh1wZbG9vgWde6ZaSgy9tXtROnPcj8MN-jZteBgwQ7g-VKyfRzyvE3kDRSEgQDz8s_XYTKn5e1_kqyYzi5Pf3BQtk4BXFihMHLDfYHH0faj7uxhu2PKAY1aVZotAWAwgJlAgTBn_o2vC5Hvpu7BtJSJgY4fxPsc5YicfmTar7iqFFiGxq9EBMrDkOqxMqvD_3nQG_552CPJLSU9MBh6EHgAWB3ve9ZZl2tLr9O2-DV_5HKrQ8u_3MKQHte5Ruhtn0UtZt0ghhjtxV_KdzUk97Xk1ljbuW_vueSlTpfOZuLtUBeJZVEFAZXeb9-eSmrF-DFSBeJziACqvPyCrN2qH45C0zYiMoK1yN3aWRczUZXMZZ5kZpfdlIGwRB6NhMxAzzcl-msvJGYbGYwFhImrkLc1bqfpEnw1B371Bt2RqVgMThGieDZL_IPV3ua46P3wPo2iSlkkt8TBpE3y4Hj9-YF5exXPEAjJ7l7i_Zev_DNbDn6IgHRCHzQ3CmtybmxzpMshLCTYUdljgadVkfnPIHqfVTUo2W4h8StOVBLTPOK0L-zXCWTjsiciV0J4sFFxginzAYdMXa6CBmLBaAI-Eauizpr3nX9hP7GfwBISDh1fJue_CSz-Jn62gcT0LvD8LpIGSb58EEB4kw04NUbj8G1ZSRKfU9Y8d4M92HbXkx482eRBwEru-7J_uX--5Ob13P-aXjf6y_BC2ZqR2gB4MCB7zyfTTRsE-OttKj5p-tUnPRyTsFxkP8doyaxMhL7sfWurizq1iKRfddp86hmP6n9nDWlt1jUKDZjtp1cPiKKdfch8GxKgORakfPV1kR\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] **Distilled next steps**\nYour overall picture is **high-risk and needs urgent in-person assessment today**: you have **continuous right-sided flank/back pain**, **visible blood in the urine**, **painful urination**, **marked fatigue**, **major unintentional weight loss**, a prior history of **renal cell carcinoma follow-up/post-nephrectomy**, and the CT pipeline returned a **strong kidney-tumor signal**. Even though the pipeline is only a **preliminary tool output**, the combination of **symptoms + prior history + scan result** is concerning enough that this should be treated as an **urgent medical problem**, not something to monitor at home.\n\n**What you should do now**\n- **Seek same-day care today**\nBest option: contact your **oncology/urology team immediately** for urgent review.\nIf that is not realistically available today, go to the **ER / urgent emergency evaluation**.\n\n- **Bring or show all of this**\nTell them clearly:\n“I have a history of kidney cancer follow-up / nephrectomy, and now I have worsening right flank pain, visible blood in urine, painful urination, severe fatigue, and 28 kg unintentional weight loss over 3 months.”\n\n- **Tests they will likely need**\nLikely urgent workup includes:\n- **review of the CT scan by a radiologist/urologist**\n- **urinalysis and urine culture**\n- **CBC**\n- **creatinine / eGFR / kidney function**\n- further **urologic / oncologic imaging review and assessment**\n\n**When to go straight to the ER immediately**\nDo **not wait** if you have any of these now:\n- **fever or chills**\n- **severe worsening pain**\n- **vomiting**\n- **inability to urinate**\n- **large clots / heavy bleeding in urine**\n- **fainting, major weakness, or shortness of breath**\n\n**Important caution**\nThis does **not confirm a diagnosis by itself**, but it is absolutely strong enough to justify **urgent medical evaluation now**.\n\nI also tried to run the formal LLM distillation tool, but that external service was unavailable just now, so I manually distilled the next steps for you from the history, symptoms, and CT pipeline result.\n\nAre you satisfied with this summary, or do you want me to help you draft a **short ER / specialist message** you can copy and send right away?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0ca29368015116040169da140217948191a467c3a7a7df81e2\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1802,"output":529,"cacheRead":28288,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":30619,"cost":{"input":0.004505,"output":0.007935,"cacheRead":0.007071999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.019511999999999998}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775899643125}}
